This is a recipe for reproducibly building a LLVM/Clang/LLD based
mingw-w64 toolchain.

Benefits of a LLVM based MinGW toolchain are:

- Support for targeting ARM/ARM64 (while GCC does support these
  architectures, it does not support Windows on ARM)
- A single toolchain targeting all four architectures (i686, x86_64,
  armv7 and arm64) instead of separate compiler binaries for each
  architecture
- Support for generating debug info in PDB format
- Support for Address Sanitizer and Undefined Behaviour Sanitizer
- Support for Control Flow Guard (-mguard=cf)

This port installs the llvm-mingw wrappers and the LLVM C++ runtime
libraries (libc++, libc++abi and libunwind) and libomp for the Windows
targets.  The Windows headers and CRT are provided by devel/mingw-w64,
the compiler-rt builtins by devel/mingw-w64-compiler-rt23, winpthreads by
devel/mingw-w64-winpthreads, and the compiler, linker and binary
utilities by devel/llvm23.
